        "writer-pushes-a-looser-declaration": ".github/workflows/twin-sweep.yml is scheduled (17 7 * * *) and its job(s) write run with contents: write on the repository that serves the governed Namespace, so a looser declaration the token pushes to main is served whole: the whole gap, until the hub gate reads the push (verify/schedules/lane.py grades a push to main by a scheduled identity as a FAIL, eco-system ticket 142a)",
        "writer-merges-or-tags-through-rest": "the same contents: write token on .github/workflows/twin-sweep.yml (write) can merge a pull request through REST, landing the same looser declaration by another door, the whole gap; a REST tag signs only this party's own artefacts and moves no price under this perspective; the union of the two is the whole gap, until the hub gate reads the merge (lane.py grades a merge made by a scheduled identity as a FAIL, ticket 142a)",
        "misleading-proposal-merged-by-a-human": "shift-left.yml job compose-check runs shift-left/tier_binding.py on every pull request, which refuses a declaration looser than the strictest priced line clamped to the floor, and shift-left.yml job compose-check recomposes the party artefact on every pull request and exits non-zero on drift against the committed composed/ tree (a compose invocation, a drift test on composed/ and a non-zero exit after it, read off the step's own run block), which refuses a hand-edited rung on this line; so a proposal a human merges through the gate serves none of the gap. A merge over a red gate is the human's act, not the twin agent's (ADR-0031 decision 1)",
        "model-step-writes-a-wrong-binding-or-forecast": "no priced line rests on a grade above 3 (party/schema.json admits appetite.pricing_threshold 2 or 3 only, and a model's claim is grade 5, which never prices), so a wrong binding or forecast a model step writes reaches no figure this composition prices"
      },
